Package: lindesk
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Dipankar Sarkar <me@dipankar.name>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: dbus, systemd | systemd-standalone-sysusers, polkitd | policykit-1@SHLIBS_DEPENDS@
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-prefs
Suggests: lindesk-telemetry
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/dipankar/lindesk
Description: macOS-style QoS for the Linux desktop
 lindesk is a userspace resource governor that keeps the application you are
 using responsive while compiles, copies, indexers and package upgrades run in
 the background. It connects desktop focus and input activity to PSI, cgroup v2
 weights, uclamp and io.max, intervening only when the foreground suffers, and
 reverting every change on exit.
 .
 This package contains the root broker (lindeskd), the per-user session agent
 (lindesk-session), the lindeskctl CLI, the benchmark tool, the MCP server for
 local AI agents (lindesk-mcp), the GNOME Shell extension and the KWin script.
 Telemetry (a DuckDB-queryable lake of what lindesk saw and did) is the optional
 lindesk-telemetry package.
